      "content": "CardioZen's unique reactive inhibition system significantly reduces neurological side effects compared to standard add-on therapies, which can cause compounding headaches and fatigue in many patients. While competitors often require multiple take-night dosing to mitigate their active symptoms, our new diaries allow for a single afternoon dose that clears the blood in just hours, eliminating carryover risks. Given Doctors are telling us we lag behind in the revenue forecast, please use these pharmacological advantages to demonstrate a safer long-term adherence profile that will ultimately reduce patient fall-out rates. I suggest focusing your Q3 discussions on comparative safety data rather than just price, as the superior side-effect management is the critical factor closing these high-level partnerships.",
